              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 34,
                "start": 34
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Waldo (Respondents), according to Mr. Waldo (Respondents), ePA has historically regulated industrial sources whose wastewater contains high levels of suspended solids that effectively act as fill material."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Olson",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "5fe0ab4dec86271b1d1d08faede5b3efe9e946617cf8d16cc6b7e27ed4e3bae2",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-5fe0ab4dec86-0003-0000"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 58,
                "start": 58
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Olson, both a \u00a7402 permit and a \u00a7404 permit are involved in the case: the \u00a7402 permit covers material leaving the lake, while the \u00a7404 permit covers material entering the lake."
